'' A UDT casting to BYTE and to DOUBLE takes, per use, the cast closest to what it meets --
'' the other operand or the destination -- and the highest-ranked when nothing is met
'' (unary, intrinsics, two UDTs). fbc's choices, measured in both declaration orders; tiko
'' always took DOUBLE: 'x + 1' was 4 and 'dim as long k = x' 3 (overload re-pick refactor).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc tests/codegen/src/numeric-cast-compound.bas -o tests/codegen/numericcastcompound.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/codegen/numericcastcompound.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  101
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  200
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2.75
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  100
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2.75
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: -2.75
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  105
